---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout
  eyebrow="Ovlira 0.4"
  title="Human design. Agent composition."
  description="A local UI toolkit that gives coding agents approved building blocks, focused guidance, and deterministic checks."
  pageTitle="Ovlira · Local UI guidance for coding agents"
>
  <div class="document-page">
    <section class="summary" aria-label="Toolkit summary">
      <div class="summary-item"><div class="summary-value">35</div><div class="summary-label">Components</div></div>
      <div class="summary-item"><div class="summary-value">6</div><div class="summary-label">Recipes</div></div>
      <div class="summary-item"><div class="summary-value">2</div><div class="summary-label">Local packages</div></div>
      <div class="summary-item"><div class="summary-value good">12/12</div><div class="summary-label">Recipe selection</div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section intro-statement" aria-labelledby="intro-purpose">
      <h2 id="intro-purpose" class="section-heading">Purpose</h2>
      <p class="record-title">Keep design decisions stable while an agent adapts the product surface.</p>
      <p class="document-copy">Ovlira separates visual design from application composition. Humans approve the components, recipes, states, and constraints. Agents retrieve only the relevant contract, then implement the domain content and behaviour in ordinary application code.</p>
      <div class="page-actions">
        <a class="primary-link" href="/install/">Install Ovlira <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="quiet-link" href="/catalogue/">Browse the catalogue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="intro-loop">
      <h2 id="intro-loop" class="section-heading">The agent loop</h2>
      <ol class="process-list">
        <li class="process-row"><span class="process-index">01</span><div><strong>Retrieve</strong><p>Search compact metadata and inspect one component or recipe.</p><code>search → inspect</code></div></li>
        <li class="process-row"><span class="process-index">02</span><div><strong>Compose</strong><p>Generate local application structure with explicit, tree-shakeable imports.</p><code>add → adapt</code></div></li>
        <li class="process-row"><span class="process-index">03</span><div><strong>Verify</strong><p>Build the project and return stable diagnostics before review.</p><code>build → check</code></div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="intro-ownership">
      <h2 id="intro-ownership" class="section-heading">Ownership</h2>
      <dl class="fields">
        <div class="field"><dt>Humans</dt><dd>Visual language, component contracts, recipes, and approval.</dd></div>
        <div class="field"><dt>Agents</dt><dd>Content, domain data, actions, routing, and application behaviour.</dd></div>
        <div class="field"><dt>Ovlira CLI</dt><dd>Retrieval, generation, metadata, and deterministic guardrails.</dd></div>
        <div class="field"><dt>Application</dt><dd>Local source, local theme overrides, and explicit runtime dependencies.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section next-row" aria-labelledby="intro-next">
      <div><h2 id="intro-next" class="section-heading">Start here</h2><p class="document-copy">Install locally, generate one screen, then let the agent work inside a bounded design contract.</p></div>
      <a class="quiet-link" href="/workflow/">View the workflow <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingLayout>
